Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, udev (>= 252), bash (>= 5.1), tomb (>= 2.13), restic (>= 0.16), systemd (>= 252), jq, rsync, openssh-client, curl, gnupg, scdaemon, pinentry-gnome3 | pinentry, cryptsetup-bin, util-linux, procps, lsof, steghide, qrencode, polkitd, dbus, adwaita-icon-theme, ca-certificates
Recommends: pcscd, fuse3, libnotify-bin
Description: Native GNOME encrypted vault and independent backup manager
 OctoVault manages encrypted local vaults and encrypted backup repositories
 through a native GTK4 interface and a matching command-line interface.
 It provides folder migration, event policies, backup schedules, snapshot
 browsing, recovery information, and file restoration.
 .
 The desktop interface runs without administrator privileges. A restricted
 system service authorizes privileged operations through PolicyKit. Secret
 configuration is encrypted using systemd credentials. Removing the package
 preserves vaults, backups, credentials, and configuration.
 .
 Maintained by Vast Development Method as part of the OctoLeo Suite.
